# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: unaligned-aes-c-line-358
why: The reference code reads and writes block words through casts of byte pointers (for example ((unsigned int *)(c+msglen))[0]),
why: which are misaligned typed accesses (undefined behaviour, UBSan "misaligned address" in CI run 45610244076). The patch moves the
why: bytes with memcpy to or from a local of the same type (helper functions added in the same file). The value is the native-order
why: word the cast read or wrote, so every output is bit-identical on every target.
file: upstream/ref/aes.c
count: 1
find: rkexp[0] = ((unsigned int *)rk)[0] ^
replace: rkexp[0] = jb_ld32(rk, 0) ^
patch: unaligned-aes-c-helpers
why: Static helper functions for the memcpy-based word accesses of the other unaligned-* patches of this file (no new symbols).
file: upstream/ref/aes.c
count: 1
find: void AESKeySteup(
replace: static __inline unsigned int jb_ld32(const void *p, size_t i) { unsigned int v; memcpy(&v, (const unsigned char *)p + 4 * i, 4); return v; } void AESKeySteup(
